{
  "category": "Manipulate Pokémon",
  "entries": [
    {
      "text": "They use hypnosis to control people and Pokémon. Tales of Gothorita leading people astray are told in every corner.",
      "version": "black"
    },
    {
      "text": "Starlight is the source of their power. At night, they mark star positions by using psychic power to float stones.",
      "version": "white"
    },
    {
      "text": "According to many old tales, it creates friends for itself by controlling sleeping children on starry nights.",
      "version": "black-2"
    },
    {
      "text": "According to many old tales, it creates friends for itself by controlling sleeping children on starry nights.",
      "version": "white-2"
    },
    {
      "text": "Starlight is the source of their power. At night, they mark star positions by using psychic power to float stones.",
      "version": "x"
    },
    {
      "text": "According to many old tales, it creates friends for itself by controlling sleeping children on starry nights.",
      "version": "y"
    },
    {
      "text": "Starlight is the source of their power. At night, they mark star positions by using psychic power to float stones.",
      "version": "omega-ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "According to many old tales, it creates friends for itself by controlling sleeping children on starry nights.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "It’s said that when stars shine in the night sky, this Pokémon will spirit away sleeping children. Some call it the Witch of Punishment.",
      "version": "sword"
    },
    {
      "text": "On nights when the stars shine, this Pokémon’s psychic power is at its strongest. It’s unknown just what link Gothorita has to the greater universe.",
      "version": "shield"
    }
  ],
